      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Ascension Parish Courthouse in Donaldsonville served as Louisiana's state capital during the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.donaldsonville-la.gov/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Donaldsonville sits on the Mississippi River, a trade artery that fueled its early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
